From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mikko Gronoff <mikko.gronoff@qt.io>
Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] v8: include limits.h for CHAR_BIT in memcopy.h

SimdMemCopy() in the NEON path uses CHAR_BIT, but memcopy.h does not
include <limits.h>/<climits> and relied on it arriving transitively.
With GCC 16's libstdc++ it no longer does, breaking arm64 builds:

  v8/src/base/memcopy.h:57:23: error: 'CHAR_BIT' was not declared
      in this scope

Include the header directly.

Upstream-Status: Pending
---
 chromium/v8/src/base/memcopy.h | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/chromium/v8/src/base/memcopy.h b/chromium/v8/src/base/memcopy.h
index 266bbe3..0693feb 100644
--- a/chromium/v8/src/base/memcopy.h
+++ b/chromium/v8/src/base/memcopy.h
@@ -5,6 +5,7 @@
 #ifndef V8_BASE_MEMCOPY_H_
 #define V8_BASE_MEMCOPY_H_
 
+#include <limits.h>
 #include <stdlib.h>
 
 #include <atomic>
